venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
# The raw parquet cache and the derived tables built from it stay out of git
# (they live on a GitHub Release, see scripts/fetch_cache.py): both are
# rebuilt weekly, and every rebuild of a binary would stay in the history.
# Odds snapshots are tracked: they are small, and their commit history is the
# audit trail.
/data/*
!/data/odds/
# ...except the run log, which is the one thing in there that is output rather
# than data. `dashboard/scripts/daily.sh:15` points it at data/odds/, inside the
# re-included directory, and `lines.yml` stages that directory unconditionally
# (`git add data/odds`). So on any commit made from a checkout that has run the
# daily script, this file goes with it. It carries absolute paths from whichever
# machine wrote it, which on this one means a username and the repo's old
# directory name, published to a repo whose whole point is being public.
/data/odds/*.log
# Licensed feeds are shown on the site but must not be republished, and this
# repo is public: Sports Game Odds' terms forbid redistributing its data as
# downloadable files, and The Odds API's are no looser. Their snapshots, and
# graded lines built from them, stay on the machine that pulled them (or go to
# a private data repo); only ESPN and generated sample files are tracked here.
/data/odds/props/*_sgo.parquet
/data/odds/games/*_sgo.parquet
/data/odds/props/*_oddsapi.parquet
/data/odds/games/*_oddsapi.parquet
/data/odds/graded/licensed/

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.vscode/*.json

# generated output
*.egg-info/
nfl_data_profile.html
data_handling/explorer/cache/

# secrets
.env

# dashboard frontend
dashboard/web/node_modules/
dashboard/web/dist/
